      "hit_at_5": true,
      "citation_precision": 1.0,
      "mode": "hybrid",
      "answer": "They chose sinusoidal positional encodings because the sinusoidal functions make it easy for the model to learn relative positions: for any fixed offset\u202fk, the encoding at position\u202fpos\u202f+\u202fk can be expressed as a linear function of the encoding at\u202fpos, which they hypothesized would help the model attend by relative positions[2].",
